        "original_id": "39eb6756-bf91-5855-80db-993f18d02022",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Władysław Grydziuszko\n- Products: Douglas SBD Dauntless, Curtiss SB2C Helldiver, Tama Maru No. 2\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Polish Army, Douglas Aircraft\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n- Events: invasion of Lae-Salamaua, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Sergeant Władysław Grydziuszko (1910–1946) was a soldier in the Polish Army during World War II.\n- Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless, an American naval scout plane and dive bomber, from 1940 through 1944.\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown damaged the Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2 off Lae, New Guinea.\n- The Curtiss SB2C Helldiver replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in United States Navy service.",
